Spec: AgentMain

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  The `agent` bin entry point: installs the rustls crypto provider, registers the common
    crate's K8s accessors into `vynil_core`, initializes env logging, then dispatches the
    nine clap sub-commands to their module owners. All operational behavior lives in the
    sub-command specs; this file owns only startup ordering and the top dispatch table.

Owns:
  ./main.rs

Exposes:
  Nothing importable: this is the bin target `agent` ([[bin]] name = `agent`,
    path = src/main.rs, doc = false). The only externally visible surface is process
    argv handling and exit codes. The ten private modules (boxes, crdgen, linting,
    package, run, service, system, template, tenant, version) are declared here;
    `linting` is NOT a sub-command — it is the lint model/checkers library consumed by
    ./package/lint.sdd.
  @Parameters — clap `Parser`, `Debug`; single @command: @Commands field; command
    attributes `author, version, about, long_about = None` and
    `propagate_version = true` (every leaf renders the crate version).
  @Commands — clap `Subcommand`, `Debug`, nine variants, `///` doc help verbatim:
    @Run(run::Parameters) `Run given git repo as a jukebox source`,
    @Crdgen(crdgen::Parameters) `generate CRDs`,
    @Package(package::Parameters) `package sub-command`,
    @System(system::Parameters) `System instance sub-command`,
    @Service(service::Parameters) `Service instance sub-command`,
    @Tenant(tenant::Parameters) `Tenant limited instance sub-command`,
    @Template(template::Parameters) `Template sub-command`,
    @Box(boxes::Parameters) `box sub-command`,
    @Version(version::Parameters) `Version sub-command`.
  @main — async entry via bare @tokio::@main.

Accepts:
  argv via clap; `--version`/`-V` renders the propagated crate version through clap,
    bypassing @Version entirely.

Returns:
  `()` — @main NEVER returns a @Result and never mints an exit code itself: success is
    the implicit 0; every failure exit is minted downstream by a sub-command dispatcher
    (@process::exit with the codes frozen in ./system/mod.sdd 1/3, ./service/mod.sdd
    1/3/4/5, ./tenant/mod.sdd 1/3/4/5, ./boxes/mod.sdd 1/1, ./package/mod.sdd 1/1/2/3/4/4,
    ./run.sdd via error 1, ./crdgen.sdd via error 2, ./template/mod.sdd 1/1/3) or by a
    panic (shell exit 101, last panic line on stderr).

Raises:
  None by design — no @Result, no @unwrap/@expect (product lane, crate lints deny them).
  clap parse failure exits 2 before any startup line runs? No: startup ORDER places
    provider/context/logging BEFORE @Parameters::parse (frozen below), so a parse error
    still pays provider install + wiring + logger init first (all silent).

Handles:
  Second crypto-provider install (rustls already had a default): @install_default's
    @Err swallowed by @ok() — deliberate idempotence against the rustls 0.23.41 no-auto-
    detection regression (code comment is the authority for that WHY).
  Sub-command failure — Display-only @tracing::error! + exit inside each dispatcher;
    @main observes only `()`.

Must:
  Run startup in this EXACT order: (1)
    @rustls::crypto::ring::default_provider().install_default().ok(); (2)
    @common::context::wire_core_k8s() — pure registration of the five context hooks into
    @vynil_core (./../common/src/context.sdd), NO cluster I/O, safe without a kubeconfig;
    (3) @env_logger::init_from_env with @filter_or `LOG_LEVEL` default `info` and
    @write_style_or `LOG_STYLE` default `auto`; (4) @Parameters::parse; (5) dispatch.
  Use the bare @tokio::@main which — FACT: workspace tokio carries `macros` +
    `rt-multi-thread` — expands to a MULTI-thread runtime with default worker count;
    `block_in_place` bridges used by common/core are legal on it (they park one worker).
  Dispatch synchronously for @Version (@run returns ()), @Run (@unwrap_or_else → exit 1,
    `Run failed with: {e:}`), @Crdgen (`CRD generation failed with: {e:}` → exit 2),
    @Template and @Package (their run fns are sync and own their exit lanes); await
    @System/@Service/@Tenant/@Box.
  Never log or exit at this level beyond what dispatch arms do inline.

Depends on:
  ./run.sdd, ./crdgen.sdd, ./package/mod.sdd, ./system/mod.sdd, ./service/mod.sdd,
    ./tenant/mod.sdd, ./template/mod.sdd, ./boxes/mod.sdd, ./version.sdd — all nine
    arms; ./../common/src/context.sdd — wire_core_k8s semantics; ./../common/src/lib.sdd
    for the shared VERSION constant surfaced by `--version` and VersionCmd alike.

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide later whether the @Run doc `Run given git repo as a jukebox source` is
      historical: @run.sdd executes ONE Rhai script given by -f, no git repo and no
      jukebox. Fix help or restore the promised behavior.
  [ ] Decide whether startup (provider/wiring/logger) should move after
      @Parameters::parse so `agent --help`/`--version`/`version` don't initialize the
      logging machinery; frozen as-is until then.
  [ ] Decide the crate-level lint attributes pair (deny unwrap/expect, warn
      arithmetic/indexing under not(test)) — identical shape across binaries; is it
      pinned by /linting.sdd as a workspace contract (cross-check pending ./../main.sdd
      siblings)?
  [ ] Cover @main with a process-level test harness (trycmd/assert_cmd style): zero
      tests exist for startup ordering, the nine-arm dispatch table, and the exit-code
      matrix above; none of the current unit tests exercise main.rs.

Done when:
  A process-level harness pins startup order, both silent-startup lanes (no kubeconfig
    needed for version/crdgen/help), and the full exit-code matrix.

Scenario: version path never touches the cluster lane
  Given `AgentMain` invoked as `… version` (or with `--version`)
  When @main runs
  Then provider install, five-hook wiring, and logger init still execute first (frozen
    order) but issue no cluster I/O (./../common/src/context.sdd: registration only),
    and @version::run prints the shared VERSION constant
  And the process exits 0

Scenario: dispatch exit codes are minted downstream only
  Given any failing sub-command
  When control leaves a dispatcher's @unwrap_or_else arm
  Then @process::exit carries that dispatcher's frozen code (no code is minted in
    @main) and @tracing::error emitted its Display-only line first
